STATEMENT 5: DeleteProductAsync() - Transaction with DELETE
============================================================================

ORIGINAL SQL SERVER STATEMENT:
BEGIN TRANSACTION;
    DECLARE @OldPrice DECIMAL(18,2);
    DECLARE @OldStock INT;
    
    SELECT @OldPrice = Price, @OldStock = StockQuantity
    FROM Products
    WHERE ProductId = @ProductId;
    
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    VALUES (@ProductId, 'DELETE', @OldPrice, NULL, @OldStock, NULL, GETDATE());
    
    DELETE FROM Products 
    WHERE ProductId = @ProductId;
    
    UPDATE ProductStats
    SET 
        TotalProducts = TotalProducts - 1,
        AveragePrice = CASE 
            WHEN TotalProducts > 1 
            THEN (AveragePrice * TotalProducts - @OldPrice) / (TotalProducts - 1)
            ELSE 0
        END,
        LastUpdated = GETDATE()
    WHERE StatId = 1;
COMMIT;

DMS TOOL OUTPUT:
Status: error (inferred from pattern)

MANUAL CONVERSION REASONING:
- Similar to Statement 4
- DELETE syntax is identical between SQL Server and PostgreSQL
- CASE statements are identical
- GETDATE() -> NOW()
- Transaction managed at ADO.NET level

POSTGRESQL CONVERTED STATEMENT (ADO.NET approach):
Execute as separate statements within NpgsqlTransaction:
1. SELECT Price, StockQuantity FROM Products WHERE ProductId = @ProductId
2. INSERT INTO ProductHistory with NOW()
3. DELETE FROM Products WHERE ProductId = @ProductId
4. UPDATE ProductStats with CASE and NOW()

Individual Statements:
